# Optional. Without this, the app runs fully offline on bundled demo data.
# Get a free key at https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api (v3 auth, "API Key").
#
# NEVER commit a real key in this file or anywhere else in the repo. For local
# development, copy this file to ".env.local" (already git-ignored) and put
# your real key there. For the deployed GitHub Pages build, add it as a
# repository secret named TMDB_API_KEY instead (see README) — the deploy
# workflow injects it as this same variable at build time.
VITE_TMDB_API_KEY=

# Optional. Without this, Google sign-in and Drive sync stay off and the app
# keeps data in this browser only. This is an OAuth Client ID for a Web
# application, not a secret - it is safe to expose in the built bundle (see
# README's "Google ile Giriş ve Drive Eşitlemesi" section for how to create
# one, including the redirect URI it needs). For the deployed GitHub Pages
# build, add it as a repository *variable* (not a secret) named
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID instead - the deploy workflow injects it as this same
# variable at build time.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
